<section class="wrap narrow pad prose">
  <h1>About HaqSetu</h1>
  <p class="lead">HaqSetu (हक़ = right, सेतु = bridge) helps every Indian citizen find the government schemes and welfare benefits they may be entitled to — regardless of state, language, education or technical knowledge.</p>
  <h2>How matching works</h2>
  <p>Each scheme in our catalogue carries its eligibility rules in a structured form — age, state, district, income, education, occupation, family circumstances and other conditions. A deterministic rules engine compares your profile with those rules and puts each scheme into one of three groups: <b>potentially eligible</b>, <b>more information required</b>, or <b>not currently eligible</b>. Every result shows exactly which conditions matched, which are unknown and which are not met.</p>
  <p>No artificial-intelligence model decides eligibility. Where an optional "explain in simple language" feature is enabled, it only rephrases the verified record and never adds rules.</p>
  <h2>Where the information comes from</h2>
  <p>Scheme information is compiled from official government sources such as <a href="https://www.myscheme.gov.in" rel="noopener">myScheme</a>, <a href="https://www.india.gov.in" rel="noopener">india.gov.in</a>, ministry and state government portals, and official notifications. Each record shows its source and its verification status. Records marked <em>awaiting verification</em> have not yet been checked by a HaqSetu reviewer.</p>
  <h2>What HaqSetu is not</h2>
  <p>HaqSetu is an independent information service. It is not a government website, does not process applications, and cannot guarantee approval. Applications are always made on official government portals or offices.</p>
</section>
